<title>UK: German refinery bid deadline delayed till end Oct.</title>
<headline>German refinery bid deadline delayed till end Oct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The deadline for bids for the 190,000 barrels per day Wilhelmshaven refinery has been postponed by one month until October 31 because potential buyers need more time, industry sources said on Tuesday. The previous deadline was September 30 but Hans van Weelden, managing director of the refinery said, &quot;The buyers needed more time to enter their bids.&quot;</p>
<p>The German refinery, which is jointly owned 50 percent each by SA Louis Dreyfus Energy Cie and Tusculum Holdings BV, is due to be sold by the end of the year.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 4984</p>
</text>
